== Title decisions ==

* '''[[Automaton]] → [[Automaton (computation)]]''' because unqualified ''automaton'' also has a durable mechanical/self-operating-machine meaning.
* [[State machine]] remains separate: it is a general state/transition model; computational automata are a major formal subclass/use.
* [[Turing completeness]] keeps the common computing title, but its Core/Technical pages must distinguish computational universality from specialized computability-theory uses such as Turing-complete sets/degrees.
* [[Computer security]] remains canonical rather than silently expanding into all cybersecurity/information-security policy.
* [[Database]] must distinguish the organized data collection from a database management system (DBMS).

== Domain decision ==

No new controlled Domain is required.

Primary Domain is '''Computer science''', with substantive cross-domain use of Mathematics, Technology, Systems science, Engineering, Philosophy, and Cognitive science where justified.

