== Source-family audit ==

* '''Stanford Encyclopedia of Philosophy''' — Turing machines, computability, Church–Turing thesis and theoretical computation.
* '''OpenDSA / formal-languages curricula''' — formal languages, automata, Turing machines and language hierarchy.
* '''ACM CS2023 curriculum''' — contemporary Computer science foundation boundaries, including architecture, OS, databases, networking and human factors.
* '''NIST CSRC / DADS''' — computer security, cryptography and state-machine terminology.
* '''Standard systems texts''' — architecture, operating systems, networks, databases, compilers and distributed systems.
* '''HCI literature / ACM''' — interaction, usability and human factors.
* '''Singer & Draper (SPLASH 2025) and Temkin''' — serious/public treatment of esoteric programming languages.
* Wikipedia/Esolang wiki are discovery/community sources only where stronger academic sources exist.

