== Phase-1 decisions ==

# Keep the wave at 17 concepts.
# Normalize [[Automaton]] to [[Automaton (computation)]].
# Keep [[State machine]] distinct from computational automata.
# Do not create a new Domain.
# Satisfy the ten existing Computer science request records during Phase 2 rather than duplicate them.
# Treat the Church–Turing thesis as a thesis connecting formal models with effective calculability, not a theorem.
# Separate computability from complexity and practical feasibility.
# Treat Turing completeness as computational universality under idealized resources, not speed or usefulness.
# Separate architecture from microarchitecture and operating systems from kernels.
# Separate databases from DBMS software.
# Separate networking substrate from distributed-system coordination.
# Separate security from cryptography and cryptography from encryption.
# Treat HCI as broader than graphical interface design.
# Retain [[Esoteric programming language]] as a legitimate public concept because current academic work treats esolangs as language-design, pedagogy and computational-culture objects, not merely jokes.

